Description:

Numeric Sieve match variable references are now required to be non-negative,
as RFC 5229 specifies, and are checked against the number of match variables
actually captured.  Previously a reference carrying a minus sign was accepted
as a number and then used as an index into the list of match variables,
reading memory from before the start of that list.

Tracked as GitHub security advisory GHSA-98j8-cw4p-2fv5.


